<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;WILLIAN GRINFIELD LELY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willian Grinfield Lely is a man of refined taste and elegance, known for his piercing blue eyes and perfect grooming. He is the epitome of sophistication and has a deep connection with George Henry Philott."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGE HENRY PHILOTT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"George Henry Philott is a man with rugged good looks and gentle demeanor, captivating Willian Grinfield Lely with his kind face and laughter. He is described as having piercing brown eyes and curly hair."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OAKWOOD MANOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oakwood Manor is a grand estate where the residents of Willowdale gather for social events, and where Willian Grinfield Lely and George Henry Philott have a deep connection."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WILLOWDALE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Willowdale is a sleepy town in the countryside, known for its rolling hills and blooming roses during the summer of 1885."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNETTE JANE MASSY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Annette Jane Massy is a member of the peerage and is married to Willian Grinfield Lely, as confirmed by multiple credible sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEPEERAGE.COM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ThePeerage.com is a reliable online genealogical resource that lists Annette Jane Massy as the wife of Willian Grinfield Lely."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURKE'S PEERAGE AND BARONETAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burke's Peerage and Baronetage is a respected publication on British nobility that confirms the marriage between Willian Grinfield Lely and Annette Jane Massy."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UK CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The UK Census of 1881 records Willian Grinfield Lely as married to Annette Jane Massy, further substantiating their union."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLLING HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rolling Hills are part of the countryside surrounding Willowdale, providing a picturesque backdrop for the events of the summer of 1885."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUMMER OF 1885&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Summer of 1885 is a specific period in time when the events of the story take place, characterized by warm weather and blooming roses."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLOOMING ROSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blooming Roses are a symbol of beauty and life, prevalent in the setting of Willowdale during the summer of 1885."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHIRPING CRICKETS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chirping Crickets are a natural sound that adds to the serene atmosphere of the countryside during the summer of 1885."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GRAND BALLROOM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Grand Ballroom is a significant space within Oakwood Manor where social events and gatherings take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FADING LIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fading Light is a descriptive element that sets the mood for the evening events in the grand ballroom."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PERFECTLY COIFFED HAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Perfectly Coiffed Hair is a detail that highlights Willian Grinfield Lely's attention to personal grooming."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TAILORED BLACK SUIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tailored Black Suit is a description of Willian Grinfield Lely's attire, emphasizing his sophistication."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERCING BLUE EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Piercing Blue Eyes are a physical attribute of Willian Grinfield Lely, contributing to his appearance and demeanor."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUGGED GOOD LOOKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rugged Good Looks are a physical attribute of George Henry Philott, highlighting his attractive appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PIERCING BROWN EYES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Piercing Brown Eyes are a physical attribute of George Henry Philott, contributing to his appearance and demeanor."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CURLY HAIR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Curly Hair is a physical attribute of George Henry Philott, adding to his distinctive appearance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHISPERED JOKE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Whispered Joke is a moment of intimacy and humor between Willian Grinfield Lely and George Henry Philott during the evening."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0128</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;WILLIAN GRINFIELD LELY&quot;" target="&quot;GEORGE HENRY PHILOTT&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Willian Grinfield Lely is deeply captivated by George Henry Philott, who makes his heart skip a beat. Their connection is palpable and hints at a deeper relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"emotional connection, attraction"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0128</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;WILLIAN GRINFIELD LELY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNETTE JANE MASSY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Willian Grinfield Lely is married to Annette Jane Massy, as confirmed by multiple credible sources including ThePeerage.com, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, and the UK Census of 1881."</data>
      <data key="d5">"marriage, legal bond"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0128</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;GEORGE HENRY PHILOTT&quot;" target="&quot;ANNETTE JANE MASSY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"There is no direct relationship mentioned between George Henry Philott and Annette Jane Massy, but both are connected to Willian Grinfield Lely, suggesting a possible indirect connection."</data>
      <data key="d5">"indirect connection, shared context"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0128</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
